  "prefLabel": "Puc 203.17 Orders Nisi",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 203.17 Orders Nisi.\n\n(a) In a docketed matter, the commission shall elect to issue a final order with a delayed effective date referred to as an order nisi.\n\n(b) If permitted under New Hampshire law.\n\n(c) The commission determines that the record is sufficient to support a commission decision without further process.\n\n(d) Any order nisi shall include a notice and publication requirement to allow interested parties an opportunity to object or request a further hearing.\n\n(e) An interested party that fails to timely intervene or participate in a proceeding shall demonstrate good cause for late-intervention, as provided by RSA 541-A:32, II.\n\nSource. #14184, eff 1-24-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc200.html"
}
